r  role in running the family business he  went to university in chicago and was  close with helen and later says that he  voted to kill them instead of her when  that came up he also brings up darlene  snell which means that the birds are now  tasked with getting her to shut down her  operation and later navarro backs him up  on this he explains that if he shows any  weakness javi could make a move to try  to take over he also tells the birds  that he wants them to set up a deal with  their fbi contacts he'll give up his  cartel but he wants to be able to move  freely between the us and mexico and  he's essentially looking for immunity  for all of his crimes they tell him that  there's no way that they can make that  happen and he reminds them that they  don't really have a choice the bright  side is that if they pull it off they'll  be free of their obligation to him and  that sets up what they have to try to do  for the rest of the season after ben's  death at the end of season three ruth  langmore stopped working for marty and  threw in with darlene and her cousin  wyatt at the beginning of season 4 she  buys the lazy o motel to launder their  money and this is where we first met her  and her cousins when the birds came to  town in season one she's got a problem  though she knows how to run marty's  laundering software but doesn't know how  to make her own this is what will  eventually lead to her teaming up with  jonah who's developed software at age 14  which is impressive even if the actor  has outgrown his role in the past couple  of years he's still upset about learning  from helen that his parents had been  killed and after wendy decides to take  the hard approach in trying to bend him  to her will he goes full team ruth for  all seven episodes on the other hand  charlotte is completely on board with  the family business and has even decided  she's going straight into it rather than  going to college beyond reaching out to  wyatt and threatening helen's daughter  erin at one point they don't give her  much to do in these episodes but i  couldn't help noticing that the actor  made a real attempt to copy some allure  lenny's mannerisms which shows how much  she's starting to take after her mother  helen's disappearance has brought  another new character to town mel is a  private investigator that says he was  hired by her husband to get her  signature on divorce paperwork he has a  habit of showing up at inopportune times  and after observing the birds for a  while he starts to believe that ben  might have been involved with helen's  disappearance of course ben is dead so  he's barking up the wrong tree but he  may turn out to be a real problem for  marty and wendy when they looked into  his past they learned that he was a cop  that was really good at his job before  his substance abuse issues led to him  getting caught in the evidence room and  losing his badge for most of the season  wendy is making big moves in her attempt  to turn them into one of the most  powerful families in the midwest and  that includes working with a  pharmaceutical company whose reputation  has taken a hit for their role in  helping to create the opioid crisis that  helped her put together a 150 million  dollar war chest after she stole jim out  from under charles wilks and made him  their full-time attorney i compared her  to walter white earlier because this has  completed her transformation that  started back in season 2. it's clear  this has all gone to her head and she  makes two questionable decisions that  will make things difficult for the  family going forward the first was to  use her brother ben for what she says is  good pr saying that he had a drug  problem and using the fact that he's  missing to her advantage this causes  problems with marty and with ruth and  that brings darlene into things to try  to stick up for wyatt's cousin the  second is that she tries to force jonah  into coming back to the family and when  that doesn'