roduction goals even while he was  withholding his product he calls claire  who tells him that marty provided a stop  gap and when pressed gives up ruth's  description things hadn't been going  good for her because darlene found out  that she did the deal with marty and had  also killed frank senior in a rage and  so ruth and wyatt were going to take off  together and she took the opportunity to  tell frank jr about what happened to his  father because wendy contacted social  services and told them about darlene's  heart attack though they were coming to  take zeke and when wyatt found out about  that he wasn't able to leave her he  decided to marry her to keep that from  happening ruth is initially upset  because they were that close to getting  out themselves but she eventually  accepts it and then has to go and tell  frank jr that he can't kill her at the  same time things take a real turn for  the birds when navarro returns to his  plane where he's surrounded by cops and  taken into custody maya went behind her  boss's back and made a move against him  and now there's nothing that they can  really do about it this worries marty  and wendy because they're afraid that  hobby's gonna think that they were  involved because maya was he sends  charlotte to go get jonah and take him  into hiding at buddy's mausoleum and  when she goes to the lazio to pick him  up mel is there and he overhears part of  their conversation while they're hiding  they do have a talk where she tries to  reassure him that they'll always stick  together and that they'll always be fine  marty and wendy are able to get the fbi  to consider a deal with hobby now that  omar is locked up they need him to  contact his nephew and tell him to do it  though and he almost kills marty before  wendy can talk him into it the plan is  that if he makes a deal then navarro  will be extradited to mexico where he  can walk away from all of this before he  leaves he warns that if he isn't out of  jail in 48 hours nelson has orders to  kill them wyatt and darlene have their  wedding at the same time the fbi is  explaining the deal to hobby it's  changed to 10 years of running the  cartel instead of 5 and includes extra  stipulations which all kind of backs up  what maya was saying and we see mel call  her on the phone after he sees her on  the news and tells her that he's a big  fan which hints at a team up in the  second half of the season darlene and  wyatt come home to find hobby waiting in  their living room now that he works for  the fbi he feels emboldened and he  shoots and kills both of them and walks  out leaving zeke crying in the  background ruth was headed over there to  give them their gift and tell them  goodbye and she's the one who discovers  the bodies she grabs zeke and drives  away crying and initially thinks it's  frank jr but when she talks to him and  realizes he didn't do it she heads  straight to the bird's house she demands  to know who killed wyatt and they're  reluctant to say anything now that  they're relying on the deal between the  fbi and hobby in one final act of  rebellion against wendy jonah tells her  and when marty pleads with her not to  get involved with hobby she screams if  you want to stop me you're gonna have to  effing kill me which you have to imagine  wendy is already considered she takes  her shotgun and storms out and gets into  her truck with zeke and takes off the  episode ends with her driving away  thinking about what she's going to do  and then breaking down screaming part  one ends with a pretty big cliffhanger  and the unresolved mystery of the car  crash at the beginning that certainly  hints at the family coming back together  enough that they're ready to get out  again but there's a lot that needs to  happen to get them there if you think  about it ruth really has lost it all now  that she's lost wyatt it's clear that  marty still has a sense of wanting to  look after her but after what happened  with ben there's no 